---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Low Ovarian Reserve & DOR"
  description="Low ovarian reserve treatment at IRFC. Expert care for diminished ovarian reserve (DOR), low AMH, and premature ovarian insufficiency across Southern California."
>
  <Nav />

  <section class="pt-40 pb-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <div class="h-px w-12" style="background: var(--color-gold-500);"></div>
          <span class="text-xs tracking-widest uppercase" style="color: var(--color-gold-600); font-family: var(--font-sans);">Conditions We Treat</span>
        </div>
        <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-serif);" class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-light text-stone-800 mb-5 leading-none">
          Low Ovarian Reserve
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-stone-500 font-light leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          A diagnosis of low ovarian reserve — diminished AMH, elevated FSH, or a low antral follicle count — is not the end of the road. At IRFC, we specialize in maximizing outcomes for patients with reduced egg supply, including through egg donation when the time is right.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20" style="background: var(--color-stone-50);">
    <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-14">
        <div>
          <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-serif);" class="text-3xl font-light text-stone-800 mb-5">Understanding Ovarian Reserve</h2>
          <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 text-sm">Every woman is born with a finite number of eggs. "Ovarian reserve" refers to the quantity and quality of eggs remaining. It naturally declines with age — but some women experience this decline earlier than expected, a condition known as diminished ovarian reserve (DOR).</p>
          <p class="text-stone-600 leading-relaxed mb-5 text-sm">DOR does not mean pregnancy is impossible — but it does mean that time is particularly important, and that treatment should be thoughtful and individualized. IRFC physicians bring extensive experience managing DOR at every stage of severity.</p>
          <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-serif);" class="text-xl font-light text-stone-800 mb-4">Key Markers We Evaluate</h3>
          <div class="space-y-3">
            {[
              { name: 'AMH (Anti-Müllerian Hormone)', desc: 'The most reliable single marker of ovarian reserve. Produced by small follicles, AMH reflects the size of the remaining egg pool.' },
              { name: 'AFC (Antral Follicle Count)', desc: 'Ultrasound count of small follicles visible at the start of a cycle — a direct measure of immediately available eggs.' },
              { name: 'FSH (Follicle-Stimulating Hormone)', desc: 'Elevated early-cycle FSH suggests the brain is working harder to recruit eggs — a sign of diminished reserve.' },
              { name: 'Estradiol (Day 3)', desc: 'Elevated early-cycle estradiol can mask FSH elevation and is assessed alongside FSH for a complete picture.' },
            ].map(m => (
              <div class="p-4 bg-white border border-stone-200">
                <p class="text-sm font-medium text-stone-800 mb-1">{m.name}</p>
                <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">{m.desc}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-5">
          <div class="p-7 bg-white border border-stone-200">
            <p class="text-xs tracking-widest uppercase mb-3" style="color: var(--color-stone-400); font-family: var(--font-sans);">Who Is Affected?</p>
            <ul class="space-y-2">
              {[
                'Women over 35 (natural age-related decline)',
                'Women with a family history of early menopause',
                'Patients who have undergone ovarian surgery (e.g., endometrioma removal)',
                'Patients after chemotherapy or radiation',
                'Women with certain autoimmune conditions',
                'Women with unexplained infertility who test poorly despite younger age',
              ].map(w => (
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-sm text-stone-600">
                  <div class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full flex-shrink-0 mt-1.5" style="background: var(--color-gold-500);"></div>
                  {w}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="p-7 bg-white border border-gold-200" style="border-color: var(--color-gold-200);">
            <p class="text-xs tracking-widest uppercase mb-2" style="color: var(--color-gold-600); font-family: var(--font-sans);">IRFC's Approach</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 leading-relaxed">We believe in honest, direct communication about prognosis — combined with creative, individualized treatment strategies that maximize every available egg. Dr. Lin and Dr. Liu are experienced managing DOR at all severity levels.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-24 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10">
      <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-serif);" class="text-3xl font-light text-stone-800 mb-10">Treatment Options for Low Ovarian Reserve</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {[
          { title: 'Optimized IVF Stimulation', desc: 'IRFC customizes stimulation protocols specifically for DOR patients — using higher doses, shorter protocols, or alternative approaches (e.g., flare or antagonist protocols) to maximize the number of eggs retrieved.' },
          { title: 'Mild / Mini-Stimulation IVF', desc: 'For some DOR patients, a gentle approach retrieving fewer but potentially higher-quality eggs may be preferable. Dr. Liu specializes in mild stimulation protocols tailored to individual response.' },
          { title: 'Egg Banking Over Multiple Cycles', desc: 'Freezing eggs or embryos from several cycles before attempting transfer can accumulate a larger pool — improving the overall chance of success for patients with very low reserve.' },
          { title: 'Natural or Modified Natural Cycle IVF', desc: 'For patients who produce very few eggs with stimulation, retrieving the single egg the body selects naturally can be a meaningful option.' },
          { title: 'PGT-A with Low Reserve', desc: 'Combining PGT-A with IVF allows selection of chromosomally normal embryos — reducing the chance of wasted transfers and miscarriage. Particularly valuable when the embryo pool is small.' },
          { title: 'Donor Egg IVF', desc: 'When a patient\'s own eggs are no longer viable, donor egg IVF offers excellent success rates. IRFC\'s comprehensive donor program, in partnership with Fairfax EggBank, provides access to a wide range of screened, tested donors.' },
        ].map(t => (
          <div class="p-7 border border-stone-200 card-hover">
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-serif);" class="text-lg font-light text-stone-800 mb-3">{t.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">{t.desc}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="relative overflow-hidden" style="height: 360px;">
    <img src="/images/patient-portrait.jpg" alt="IRFC fertility patient" class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center" />
    <div class="absolute inset-0" style="background: linear-gradient(to left, rgba(20,18,15,0.5) 0%, transparent 60%);"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-end px-10 lg:px-20">
      <p style="font-family: var(--font-serif);" class="text-2xl font-light text-white max-w-sm leading-relaxed text-right">
        A low reserve is not the end of your story.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16" style="background: var(--color-stone-50);">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 text-center">
      <svg class="w-8 h-8 mx-auto mb-6 opacity-20" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 32 32" style="color: var(--color-gold-600);"><path d="M10 8C6.686 8 4 10.686 4 14v10h10V14H8c0-1.1.9-2 2-2V8zm16 0c-3.314 0-6 2.686-6 6v10h10V14h-6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2V8z"/></svg>
      <p style="font-family: var(--font-serif);" class="text-2xl font-light text-stone-700 italic leading-relaxed mb-5">"When I was 41, Dr. Lin was honest with me. He said I had about a 10% chance. He designed a protocol around that reality — and my baby is now 6 months old."</p>
      <p class="text-xs tracking-widest uppercase" style="color: var(--color-gold-600);">— IRFC Patient, Age 41, IVF with DOR</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-screen-xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-10 text-center">
      <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-serif);" class="text-4xl font-light text-stone-800 mb-4">Act Early, Act with Expertise</h2>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: var(--color-stone-500);">With low ovarian reserve, timing matters. Our physicians will give you an honest picture of your situation — and every available option to move forward with confidence.</p>
      <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary">Schedule a Consultation</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
